    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104016" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῑμώρ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>act of vengeance</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. Κορινθίων εἰς Σαμίους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.860a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>penalty</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διπλᾶ . . ἔστω τὰ τ. τῷ ὀφλόντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					866b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				363e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>aid, succour</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ Μενέλεω
				τιμωρήματα</span>
			<i>succour given</i> to him, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.169
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μενέλεῳ</span>
		Wesseling).</div>
